ac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & \\frac{∂f}{∂y}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y,\\, & \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡y & \\frac{{x}^{3}}{y}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=1,\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{1}{e}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe tangent to $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nz-f(a)={f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nz-1=[\\begin{aligned}3 & \\frac{1}{e}\\end{aligned}]([\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ e\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n1+3+\\frac{1}{e}=\\frac{4e+1}{e}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d61a415498a477cf836fbf5a14ce7eaf882f3864890ae27ce96fcca46040745"} {"question" "q-163058" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3a1db6fdfde8715aef4b8c8b0ff8d9dd30aef5b7de7ea9156c005383e0c5306"} {"question" "q-163058" "field" "selection" 