 the following:\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}}\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFirst, we compute the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{1})+{x}_{2})=\\frac{1}{{x}_{1}},\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}(\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}_{1})+{x}_{2})=1 \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{1}}({x}_{2}^{2}+1)=0,\\, & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & =\\frac{∂}{∂{x}_{2}}({x}_{2}^{2}+1)=2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nEvaluating $f$ and its derivative at $x=a=[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}],$ we have\n\n$$\nf(a)=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],\\,{f}^{′}(a)=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThe linear approximation of $f$ at $x=a$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x)≈f(a)+{f}^{′}(a)(x-a).\n$$\n\nSubstituting $f(a),$ ${f}^{′}(a),$ and $a$ in the equation above, we obtain\n\n$$\nf(x)≈[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-1} & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}](x-[\\begin{aligned}e \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]).\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the missing values is\n\n$$\n0+{e}^{-1}+(-2)={e}^{-1}-2.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/state.json" "file_sha256" "0d61a415498a477cf836fbf5a14ce7eaf882f3864890ae27ce96fcca46040745"} {"question" "q-163093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14068404/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3a1db6fdfde8715aef4b8c8b0ff8d9dd30aef5b7de7ea9156c005383e0c5306"} {"question" "q-163093" "field" "se